WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.375
Cutover happens one group of users at a
time, as each group moves to Entra ID.

2
00:00:05.375 --> 00:00:11.134
Before a group cuts over, acceptance tests
in plain business language are signed:

3
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:13.540
a new hire, a transfer, a separation,

4
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:17.150
leave without pay, a cancelled
action, a conversion.

5
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:20.630
Anything that could leave a
separated person with access,

6
00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:23.312
or lock out someone
active, stops the cutover.

7
00:00:23.312 --> 00:00:26.984
Then there's a dry run on real
data with no changes written,

8
00:00:26.984 --> 00:00:28.624
and a rollback plan ready.

9
00:00:28.624 --> 00:00:32.763
For seven days afterward, every
change must trace back to HR.

10
00:00:32.763 --> 00:00:35.551
When that holds, the ticket path closes.

11
00:00:35.551 --> 00:00:38.625
Nobody requests an account
for a new hire anymore.

12
00:00:38.625 --> 00:00:42.375
HR, the ISSO and the business owner sign.

13
00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.850
How will you know it works?
